      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lucama’s name comes from the first two letters of Lucy, Carrie, and Mary, three local women honored by Josephus Daniels in 1883.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucama%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic Lucama Motor Speedway, a dirt track that has drawn racing fans since 1954, still turns heads on the local circuit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/north-carolina_lucama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lucama’s downtown core earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 1986 as the Lucama Municipal Historic District.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucama%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in Lucama in 1884, and the town was officially incorporated five years later in 1889.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucama%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
